1243	\begin{lemma}[Consistency of the constructed paired-line measurement]
1244		\label{lem:combined-line-measurement-consistency}
1245		\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.combined_line_measurement_consistency}
1246		\leanok
1247		\uses{lem:qld-4-10, lem:qld-comm-line-cons, lem:pasting,
1248			def:concrete-paired-line-measurement, def:consistency,
1249			thm:qld-conditioned-polynomial-bound}
1250		This is a formalization-only construction theorem. Fix a polynomially small
1251		function $\delta_Q(\eps)$. There is a function
1252		$\delta_P(\eps,md/q)=\poly(\eps,md/q)$, in the corrected sum sense,
1253		such that for every projective strategy passing with error $\eps$ and
1254		every joint point family satisfying the conclusions of
1255		Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-10} with error $\delta_Q(\eps)$, the concrete POVM
1256		\[
1257			T^{\ell_X,\ell_Z}_{f_X,f_Z}
1258			=\hat M^{(\mathrm{Line},X),\ell_X}_{f_X}
1259			 \hat M^{(\mathrm{Line},Z),\ell_Z}_{f_Z}
1260			 \hat M^{(\mathrm{Line},X),\ell_X}_{f_X}
1261		\]
1262		has evaluated consistency defect at most $\delta_P(\eps,md/q)$ with that
1263		joint point family, averaged over two independent line-point samples,
1264		for every directed opposite placement.
1265	
1266		The two measurements are compared on the completed answer alphabet
1267		$(\F_q\cup\{\bot\})^2$. An outcome $(f_X,f_Z)$ of $T^{\ell_X,\ell_Z}$ is
1268		postprocessed to the pair of evaluations of $f_X$ and $f_Z$ at the two
1269		sampled points, with $\bot$ recorded in a coordinate whose polynomial
1270		admits no evaluation at its point. The joint point family is extended to
1271		the same alphabet by the inclusion $\F_q\subseteq\F_q\cup\{\bot\}$ in each
1272		coordinate, so it assigns the zero operator to every answer having $\bot$
1273		in a coordinate. The quantity bounded is therefore the full off-diagonal
1274		defect on $(\F_q\cup\{\bot\})^2$: pairs in which a line evaluation is
1275		undefined while the point family answers in $\F_q$ contribute to it, and
1276		it is not the summation over answers in $\F_q$ alone.
1277	
1278		The line-error function is chosen after $\delta_Q$ and its polynomial
1279		bound. This isolates the consistency part of the preceding construction
1280		while retaining its defining measurement; see
1281		\cite{gap:qpbt_subline-claims-line-marginal}.
1282	\end{lemma}
